# {{ project_name }}

{{ description }}

This repository was bootstrapped from `gh:copier-templates/base`. It is intentionally small: baseline repository hygiene for language-agnostic projects — line endings, ignore rules, and local quality checks without imposing a language stack.

## What It Adds

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `.editorconfig` | LF, UTF-8, final newline, per-language indents |
| `.gitattributes` | Text normalization, binary marking |
| `.gitignore` | `macOS` + `mise` + `.env` ignores |
| `prek.toml` | Safety checks, secrets scanning, shell lint/format, conventional commits |
| `.shellcheckrc` | Bash dialect, extra checks |
| `mise.toml` | Pinned tools (`git-cliff`, `gitleaks`, `prek`, `shellcheck`, `shfmt`); `install` / `check` / `format` / `changelog` tasks |
| `cliff.toml` | Conventional-commit changelog config |
| `.github/workflows/check.yml` | CI running `mise run check` on push/PR |
| `.env.example` | Committed example for mise-loaded `.env` |
| `scripts/` | Shell scripts (shebang + `.sh` extension enforced) |

## Included Tooling

Tool versions are managed with `mise`.

- `git-cliff` for changelog generation
- `gitleaks` for secret scanning
- `prek` for local hook execution
- `shellcheck` for shell script linting
- `shfmt` for shell script formatting (`mise run format`)

## Usage

After generation, the setup tasks already ran (`git init`, `mise run install`) and committed everything as `chore: Bootstrapping project from copier template`. To verify:

```bash
mise run validate
```

## Updating from the template

Answers are stored in `.copier-answers.yml` (committed). To pull in later template changes:

```bash
copier update --trust
```

Note: updates overwrite template-owned files (`README.md`, `mise.toml`, `prek.toml`, `.gitignore`, etc.).
